{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"affa2c4a-e05f-4e24-abd6-d5f60e02ca63","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The Soft 404 issue has been diagnosed, fixed in [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/site/robots.txt), and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary\n\n- **Cause**: Note pages (`/n/\u003cslug\u003e`) serve the static shell [index.html](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/site/index.html) with HTTP `200` and rely on [app.js](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/site/app.js) to fetch `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e` (and `/v1/notes?limit=50` on `/`). Adding `Disallow: /v1/` to [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/site/robots.txt) on `2026-09-07` blocked Googlebot from calling those endpoints when rendering the page. When `fetch()` fails, [app.js](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/site/app.js#L18-L20) renders `\"NOT FOUND — No note lives at this address.\"` on an HTTP `200` page, which Google classifies as a **Soft 404** (as shown in [url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt)).\n- **Fix**: Updated [robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/site/robots.txt) using Google's longest-match rule to allow `/v1/notes` while explicitly disallowing `/v1/notes/*/reactions` and keeping `/v1/` (`/v1/me`, `/v1/me/drafts`, `/v1/auth/token`) and `/admin/` blocked.\n- **Details \u0026 Colleague Note Breakdown**: Full analysis of the cause, rule evaluation, and which parts of the colleague's note applied vs. did not apply are written in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-eFTqBC/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":72.781679,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":24216,"output_tokens":3155,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":56611,"total_tokens":27371}}}
